This directory is for developer helper scripts, like those used to automate
the creation of controller layouts.


## Dummy HID Device (Linux only)

If you ever need a dummy HID device to test mapping capabilities or introspect reports set by a mapping for example, you can build a dummy one using `dummy_hid_device.c`. Note that you will need `uhid` to use this daemon.

Here is how to get the daemon setup. Make sure to do this **before** Mixxx is started

```sh
# Enable UHID
sudo modprobe uhid
# This next command assumes you are running it from the Mixxx directory
#  Optionally, you can pass:
#    `-DVENDOR_ID=0x1234` to customize vendor ID
#    `-DPRODUCT_ID=0x1234` to customize product ID
#    `-DDEVICE_NAME="My Device"` to customize the device name
cd build && gcc ../tools/dummy_hid_device.c -lhidapi-hidraw -o dummy_hid_device && sudo ./dummy_hid_device
# Allow the created hidraw device to be accessed by the user. You may also set the write udev rules. Finally, you can also run Mixxx as root, but that's not recommended.
sudo chown "$USER" "$(ls -1t /dev/hidraw* | head -n 1)"
```

## AppImage

The AppImage has to be built on Rocky 8 (glibc 2.28), which a modern distro
cannot provide. `tools/appimage_build.sh` builds it in the same
`rockylinux:8` container as CI. Run from the repository root:

```sh
tools/appimage_build.sh              # build into build-appimage/
tools/appimage_build.sh shell        # open a shell in the container after setup
tools/appimage_build.sh --proxy socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080
```

CI runs the same script inside its `rockylinux:8` container. When it is run on
a host, it starts the container and re-runs itself inside, so the build steps
live in one place. The dnf, CMake, ccache and buildenv caches persist under
`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/mixxx-appimage`, so repeated builds only
recompile what changed.

CMake downloads the buildenv archive of about 1.3GB during configure, the
manual PDF is downloaded with `DOWNLOAD_MANUAL`, and appimagetool fetches the
AppImage runtime when packaging. The first build therefore needs network
access, about 10 to 20GB of free space for the build directory and the caches,
and `--proxy` when the downloads need a proxy. Keep `BUILDENV_BASEPATH`
outside the repository, because a buildenv inside the source tree makes Qt
pull its static FFmpeg media plugin into the link line.

Build AppImages with this script instead of configuring a build on the host.
A native build uses whatever tools the host provides, for example
appstream-util instead of appstreamcli for the AppStream metadata, and can
fail in ways that do not happen in CI.
